WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.861
<v Leo>POL-09, anti-harassment, is approved.

00:00:03.881 --> 00:00:05.134
<v Leo>So we're done, right?

00:00:05.154 --> 00:00:06.461
<v Ava>Approved isn't live.

00:00:06.481 --> 00:00:09.686
<v Ava>Thirteen countries take a little choreography first.

00:00:10.336 --> 00:00:13.335
<v Ava>Every policy is one global document plus country

00:00:13.355 --> 00:00:16.532
<v Ava>addenda that only cover what local law changes.

00:00:16.552 --> 00:00:20.649
<v Leo>So not thirteen separate copies, each called final_v7?

00:00:20.669 --> 00:00:21.270
<v Ava>Nope.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:25.332
<v Ava>One source, with local differences marked and translated where needed.

00:00:25.982 --> 00:00:27.449
<v Ava>Four countries add gates.

00:00:27.469 --> 00:00:30.655
<v Ava>In Germany, the works council co-determines conduct rules,

00:00:30.675 --> 00:00:32.331
<v Ava>so you need its agreement.

00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:33.197
<v Leo>And China?

00:00:33.217 --> 00:00:35.155
<v Leo>I'm guessing an email won't cut it.

00:00:35.175 --> 00:00:37.489
<v Ava>China needs democratic consultation.

00:00:37.509 --> 00:00:40.350
<v Ava>Vietnam registers internal labor regulations,

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:44.088
<v Ava>and Taiwan files work rules with the labor authority.

00:00:44.738 --> 00:00:49.199
<v Ava>These gates take weeks, so plan backwards from your go-live date and start early.

00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:50.503
<v Leo>And mind the calendar.

00:00:50.523 --> 00:00:55.204
<v Leo>Year-end freeze, then Lunar New Year and Tet from February 5 to 14.

00:00:55.224 --> 00:00:55.850
<v Ava>Right.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:00.211
<v Ava>Finish China, Taiwan and Vietnam before that break, or your launch slips.

00:01:00.861 --> 00:01:04.627
<v Ava>On launch day, publish in the Policy guide with an effective date,

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:06.760
<v Ava>then communicate, managers first.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.114
<v Leo>Then the hard part: getting people to actually read it.

00:01:10.134 --> 00:01:13.030
<v Ava>Collect acknowledgments, then file the evidence:

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.863
<v Ava>acknowledgment reports, filings and consultation minutes.

00:01:17.513 --> 00:01:19.934
<v Leo>Wait, why is Vietnam still in review?

00:01:19.954 --> 00:01:22.011
<v Ava>It's waiting on the authority's receipt.

00:01:22.031 --> 00:01:24.268
<v Ava>Once that's attached, the gate is cleared.

00:01:24.288 --> 00:01:26.555
<v Leo>So now I can set everything to Live?

00:01:26.575 --> 00:01:29.417
<v Ava>Now you can: every country's evidence is filed.

00:01:29.437 --> 00:01:31.107
<v Ava>That's what auditors sample.

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:35.611
<v Ava>One global policy, local gates planned early, evidence filed.

00:01:35.631 --> 00:01:36.915
<v Ava>That's what live means.

00:01:36.935 --> 00:01:38.071
<v Leo>That's the series.

00:01:38.091 --> 00:01:42.595
<v Leo>Now go update your items, and maybe rename final_v7.
